/-
# Full-paper mathematical import surface

The imports assemble the headline theorems, arbitrary natural/real cutoff
mixtures, the quantitative appendix, actual moving-rough adapters, rounded
extensions, sharp finite auxiliaries and the named examples. No theorem or
additional hypothesis is declared in this convenience module.

The prime endpoints retain their explicit arithmetic conjectures. The rough
endpoints use the proved arithmetic supplier with their stated deterministic
threshold budgets. Generic S/T consumers keep their own stated hypotheses;
importing such an interface is not a proof of those hypotheses.

Build and trust instructions are in the Lean README. Neither the existence
of this import surface nor an old artifact certifies the current sources.
Use `Paper` and `PaperAudit` for the full release scope.
-/

